 "kind": "wallclock",
 "description": "Native timing inside lang-lab-wasm:c, pinned with taskset to one vCPU, benchmarks one at a time, each repetition running every (column, size) pair in a fresh random order. L is a per-benchmark size larger than the spec sizes (see checks.clangDifferentialMsAtL); the gate requires every column to print clang's checksum at L. Two passes (C, D) with the study's binding runtime flags, 25 repetitions each, pooled.",
 "estimator": "user CPU time, because about half of the wall time was run-queue wait on a loaded host (checks.runQueueShareOfWallAtL); the two passes agree (checks.passCvsD) and the verdict also holds on wall time (stats.*.wallSpearman/wallR2Log)",
 "ratioMeaning": "numerator / denominator (lower is better); timeRatio and instrRatio are both differentials. spearman and r2Log: how well instrRatio tracks timeRatio across benchmarks (higher is better)",
 "caveats": [
  "absolute times are not quoted: the Docker VM has no steal-time accounting, so user time may include host preemption",
  "passes A and B used the pre-final runtime flags; their wasmtime time geomeans are in checks.wasmtimeTimeGeomeanByPass"
 ],
